{"game": "redfall", "language": "english", "appid": 1294810, "month": "2024-05", "window": 3, "start_date": 1715817600, "end_date": 1716508799, "month_true_total": 75, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-09-02 17:05:37 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "165768558", "author": {"steamid": "76561199073217883", "personaname": "Elkduud", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Elkduud/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 5, "playtime_forever": 769, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 426, "last_played": 1744938970, "avatar": "931cde06bac65893c1d32ba23759fb6dfdb1c708"}, "language": "english", "review": "I love this game. It launched incomplete last year and that's Xbox's fault. But the game now has 60 fps on consoles and i jumped back in. I loved my 30 hours with it on xbox so I bought it again on pc so i could play it on my steam deck. Its a pretty chill coop game if you want it to be, or you can bump up the difficulty for more of a challenge. It has its moments of horror like unscripted jump scares  when a vampire will float pass a window or appear behind you. The challenge is there also...3 or 4 vampires chasing you into a house will do it. \n\nI wanted this game to get a big expansion so bad. But now xbox has shut down the studio....however...its still a fun time and Arkane is adding offline mode to it with their last update coming soon. It will also offer up some more quality of life changes. I really disagree with all the hate the game has received. If more people gave it a chance again, they would see its a fun game that had tons of potential.", "timestamp_created": 1716252234, "timestamp_updated": 1716252234, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 6, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.454369604587554932", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_dat